3	 *
4	 * MCP (Model Context Protocol) client side for the xiaozhi voice app.
5	 * See xiaozhi_mcp.h for an overview.
6	 *
7	 * The cloud sends MCP JSON-RPC requests inside WebSocket text frames:
8	 *
9	 *   { "type": "mcp", "payload": <jsonrpc request> }
10	 *
11	 * This module is a *client*: it spawns a local MCP server ("mcp_server",
12	 * a built-in NuttX program) as a subprocess and forwards each cloud
13	 * request to it over the server's stdin pipe, then reads the server's
14	 * response from its stdout pipe and relays it back to the cloud as:
15	 *
16	 *   { "type":"mcp", "session_id":<sid>, "payload": <jsonrpc response> }
17	 *
18	 * The stdio transport uses newline-delimited JSON (one JSON-RPC object per
19	 * line, no embedded newlines), matching the MCP stdio spec and the
20	 * reference mcp-calculator-main/mcp_pipe.py bridge.
21	 *
22	 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
23	 ****************************************************************************/
