/****************************************************************************
 * apps/examples/mcp_server/mcp_server_main.c
 *
 * A local MCP (Model Context Protocol) server speaking the stdio transport.
 * It exposes a single tool, "start_app", that launches a built-in NuttX
 * application on the device via posix_spawn().
 *
 * Transport (per the MCP stdio spec): messages are newline-delimited JSON-RPC
 * 2.0 objects — one request per line on stdin, one response per line on
 * stdout, no embedded newlines. stderr is used for logging only.
 *
 * This process is spawned by the xiaozhi_voice app, which acts as the MCP
 * client and forwards the cloud's MCP requests to this server over its
 * stdin/stdout pipes.
 *
